## Hunk 3 — §7 `[reconstructed]`

```diff
@@ §7  ECHO CONTROL @@
   Structural properties that hold echo rate down:
-  · bank entries never indexed
-  · index and ordinal replies rejected
+  · bank entries never indexed
+  · entries generic enough that selection under-resolves rather
+    than misresolves
   · own-words line primary
   · [N/A] capped at twelve words
+
+  Note: ordinal rejection previously contributed here and has been
+  removed (G.3b). Echo will run higher than the pre-G.3b draft
+  assumed. What the remaining properties guarantee is that an
+  echoed value is coarse, not wrong — the accepted trade, not a
+  suppression claim.
```

That note is the substantive edit in this diff. Without it §7 reads as though the safeguards still suppress echo at the old rate, which they don't.

---

## Collision found

Not numbering — `G.3b` is replaced in place, so no renumbering cascades. The problem is **glossed cross-references**. Three sites cite `G.3b` with a parenthetical that now states the opposite of the clause:

| Site | Current gloss | Needs |
|---|---|---|
| §7 echo list | `(G.3b, rejected)` | removed by Hunk 3 |
| §D.9a, no-new-noun para | `see G.3b — examples are not values` | reword: examples are not values *absent selection* |
| §8 or §9 handoff table | `ordinal → open:` | `ordinal → populate` |

The first is handled. The other two I can't patch blind — they're the `[reconstructed]` risk, and getting the D.9a one wrong would leave the no-new-noun rule citing an inverted authority, which is worse than leaving it alone.

## Dependency to verify

G.3b positional matching counts against an order it calls "fixed and alphabetical." My record of G.3a says *fixed*; I'm less sure it says *alphabetical*. If it only says fixed, then "the third one" has an anchor per-render but no stated rule, and two renders of the same bank could differ. Either G.3a gains the word or G.3b drops the claim and relies on fixed alone — I'd take the former, it's one word and it makes positional matching mechanical rather than incidental.

## Changelog

```
G.3b  Replaced. Ordinal and index replies no longer rejected;
      identification of a bank entry populates the slot directly.
      Rejection form conflated affirmative selection with silence.
      Narrowing variant (G.3b′, proposed) declined: narrowing a
      valid generic answer is refinement, not discovery, and falls
      outside Goal's question budget. Under-resolution accepted at
      this layer. Referential matching bounded to exactly-one to
      keep matching mechanical rather than plausibility-based.
§7    Echo-control basis narrowed; see note in clause.
```

